@tradition paddle-club
// W3 rec deck words. Wednesdays 18:30-19:30 from Day 3, the river hall; Chief Holt. The slow loop; the fast run arrives with White water's integration (lead 17's call 3).
== mail
- Paddle club tomorrow, {time} in the river hall. Chief Holt takes you round the slow loop. Helmets on, everyone, no exceptions.
== ask
- Paddle club tonight. Holt watches the water like a hawk. It's oddly calming.
- Coming paddling? The slow loop, then a cup of tea on the beach.
== here
- Paddle on the left. Now the right. Now stop going in circles.   #funny
- Helmet straight. Holt will check.
- Steady. Watch the water. It tells you first.
== thanks
- You take a kayak from the dock and fall in behind Chief Holt round the slow loop. He nods. That's a lot, from him.   #warm
== chatter
- Holt said "adequate" at paddle club. To me! I've told everyone.   #funny
- Paddle club's good for the arms. Mine are still complaining.
- Holt's been paddling for years. He'll never say how many.
